      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! Here are some scenario-based questions to consider:\n\n1. **Interpersonal Relationships**: Imagine you have a group of friends and decide to take a secret trip to the city. The group plans to disobey speeding tickets, jaywalk in unfamiliar neighborhoods, and have a spontaneous get-together with impromptu activities. How comfortable are you with this plan?\n   \n2. **Problem-Solving and Innovation**: You need to quickly fix a broken-down vehicle on a busy street with minimal tools. You consider options like seeking help, improvising with the available tools, or finding an alternative route. Which approach do you choose and why?\n   \n3. **Risk Taking**: You see a young child crossing the street outside of crosswalks, while you wait for a bus. Would you:\n   a. Continue waiting at the crosswalk,\n   b. Shout or call the child's attention, or\n   c. Ignore it and continue to your destination?\n\n4. **Community Engagement**: A local community event requires a shortlist of participants for an initiative aimed at improving neighborhood safety. You're on the committee, and you have to decide whom to include. Would you prioritize:\n   a. Recent residents with practical knowledge of local",
